<Base path="/iepl-iplc-private-leased-circuits">
<div class="desktop xypufxb"><div class="site-header-slot header-slot" data-pagefind-ignore><Header /></div><div class="gradient-wrap xdq9s7f"><section class="hero xe4wmfc"><div class="padding xi9ijje fb"><div class="content xbnoz9m"><div class="head-content xhvkom8"><h1 class="xcrvchq">IEPL and IPLC Private Leased Circuits Across the Pacific</h1><p class="xrfba8c">Dedicated point-to-point capacity between two fixed endpoints, reserved for you alone and never routed over the public internet. Vocom provisions IEPL and IPLC circuits on cross-Pacific and Asia-Pacific routes, sized from sub-1 Gbps access links up to 10 Gbps and above.</p><div class="button-group x945lzz"><a class="button-primary xemwtuy" href="/vocom-international#service"><p class="xc4cgop">Explore Our Solutions</p></a><a class="button-secondary xc3hwkb fb" href="/contact-vocomai"><p class="xowcorr">Contact Us</p></a></div></div><div class="under xj1meuj"><div class="video xg7c5ze"><video class="video-fill" data-src="/assets/video/about-4b466c.mp4" data-autoplay loop muted playsinline preload="none" style="object-fit:cover;border-radius:20px;"></video></div></div></div></div></section><div class="partners xdzkk5w"><div class="xre1bfe"><div class="xrq1fly fb"></div><p class="x0jrv5i">Direct carrier and NNI partners across Asia, the Americas and Europe</p><div class="xrq1fly fb"></div></div><div class="content xerscxd"><div class="logos x2udtsx"><div class="x1zycko"><img class="fill-img" src="/assets/img/foxconn-logo-vocom-manufacturing-partner-0cda45.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></div><div class="xk5l9or"><img class="fill-img" src="/assets/img/supermicro-logo-vocom-hardware-partner-80142e.png" srcset="/assets/img/supermicro-logo-vocom-hardware-partner-80142e-512w.webp 512w, /assets/img/supermicro-logo-vocom-hardware-partner-80142e.png 916w" sizes="(min-width: 810px) and (max-width: 1199.98px) 100vw, (max-width: 809.98px) 100vw, 100vw" width="916" height="471" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></div><div class="x0ca6w1"><img class="fill-img" src="/assets/img/serverfarm-logo-vocom-data-center-partner-68e9fe.svg" width="323" height="186" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></div><div class="bizlink xljmqbv"><img class="fill-img" src="/assets/img/bizlink-logo-dd15dd.png" srcset="/assets/img/bizlink-logo-dd15dd-512w.webp 512w, /assets/img/bizlink-logo-dd15dd.png 800w" sizes="(min-width: 810px) and (max-width: 1199.98px) 100vw, (max-width: 809.98px) 100vw, 100vw" width="800" height="178" alt="BizLink logo" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></div><div class="ats xm0p1kr"><img class="fill-img" src="/assets/img/american-tech-supply-logo-98e806.png" srcset="/assets/img/american-tech-supply-logo-98e806-512w.webp 512w, /assets/img/american-tech-supply-logo-98e806.png 711w" sizes="(min-width: 810px) and (max-width: 1199.98px) 100vw, (max-width: 809.98px) 100vw, 100vw" width="711" height="104" alt="American Tech Supply logo" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></div><div class="wesco xvfe9n3"><img class="fill-img" src="/assets/img/wesco-logo-vocom-fiber-optic-supply-chain-partner-f1eba4.png" srcset="/assets/img/wesco-logo-vocom-fiber-optic-supply-chain-partner-f1eba4-512w.webp 512w, /assets/img/wesco-logo-vocom-fiber-optic-supply-chain-partner-f1eba4.png 559w" sizes="(min-width: 810px) and (max-width: 1199.98px) 100vw, (max-width: 809.98px) 100vw, 100vw" width="559" height="357" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></div></div></div></div><div class="cards x3cvuhv"><div class="h2 xlsdbpm"><div class="xf8fnkf"><h3 class="h3 xk0nmq5"><span class="xgvztuw">How to Order a Private Circuit</span></h3><p class="xq9pbwc">Two endpoints and a bandwidth figure are enough to start:</p></div></div><div class="xznektj"><div class="x1ai5nw"><div class="xepe0jq"><div class="placeholder xlz1oqk"><img class="fill-img" src="/assets/img/placeholder-image-4daa70.jpg" srcset="/assets/img/placeholder-image-4daa70-512w.webp 512w, /assets/img/placeholder-image-4daa70-1024w.webp 1024w, /assets/img/placeholder-image-4daa70.jpg 1920w" sizes="(min-width: 810px) and (max-width: 1199.98px) 100vw, (max-width: 809.98px) 100vw, 100vw" width="1920" height="1280" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></div><div class="p2 xamhnmh"><div class="xzzn7mt"><p class="x19p4ct">Step 1: Send Your Endpoints</p><p class="xagxmxk">The two locations, the bandwidth you need now, and where you expect it to be in three years.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="xjlmtdo fb"><div class="material x2at3tf"><svg fill="rgb(166, 166, 166)" width="100%" height="100%" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="m12 4-1.41 1.41L16.17 11H4v2h12.17l-5.58 5.59L12 20l8-8z"/></svg></div></div><div class="xxlpcrb"><div class="xepe0jq"><div class="placeholder xlz1oqk"><img class="fill-img" src="/assets/img/vocom-ai-enterprise-tools-for-coaching-security-and-c516b5.jpg" srcset="/assets/img/vocom-ai-enterprise-tools-for-coaching-security-and-c516b5-512w.webp 512w, /assets/img/vocom-ai-enterprise-tools-for-coaching-security-and-c516b5-1024w.webp 1024w, /assets/img/vocom-ai-enterprise-tools-for-coaching-security-and-c516b5.jpg 1280w" sizes="(min-width: 810px) and (max-width: 1199.98px) 100vw, (max-width: 809.98px) 100vw, 100vw" width="1280" height="960" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></div><div class="p2 xamhnmh"><div class="xzzn7mt"><p class="x19p4ct">Step 2: Get a Sized Route</p><p class="xagxmxk">An engineer returns the route, protection and latency for the path, not just a rate card.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="double xrnfdt3"><div class="simple-left-points xnvm0ta"><div class="h2 xlsdbpm"><div class="xrebnwx"><h3 class="h3 xk0nmq5"><span class="xgvztuw">Why Choose </span><span class="xwgkw2u">Vocom</span><span class="xgvztuw">?</span></h3><p class="xq9pbwc">Private capacity on a backbone we run, not resold transport:</p></div></div><div class="x2yd3zd"><div class="xmlpigy"><div class="p2 xuszldq"><p class="xspwoe5">Facilities-Based, Not a Reseller</p></div><div class="xkcikp3"><div class="bullet-point x6idugm"><div class="icon xyojafn"><div class="material x8n8qcu"><svg fill="rgb(120, 120, 120)" width="100%" height="100%" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M9 16.17 4.83 12l-1.42 1.41L9 19 21 7l-1.41-1.41z"/></svg></div></div><p class="xv3l5jr">FCC 214 licensed international carrier since 1998</p></div><div class="bullet-point x6idugm"><div class="icon xyojafn"><div class="material x8n8qcu"><svg fill="rgb(120, 120, 120)" width="100%" height="100%" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M9 16.17 4.83 12l-1.42 1.41L9 19 21 7l-1.41-1.41z"/></svg></div></div><p class="xv3l5jr">Hundreds of direct carrier and NNI relationships</p></div><div class="bullet-point x6idugm"><div class="icon xyojafn"><div class="material x8n8qcu"><svg fill="rgb(120, 120, 120)" width="100%" height="100%" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M9 16.17 4.83 12l-1.42 1.41L9 19 21 7l-1.41-1.41z"/></svg></div></div><p class="xv3l5jr">24/7 NOC monitoring across every business line</p></div></div><a class="link-button xzjxv9b" href="/vocom-services"><p class="x9uyvup">See Our Network Coverage</p><div class="material x3b1erb"><svg fill="rgb(13, 13, 13)" width="100%" height="100%" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M16.01 11H4v2h12.01v3L20 12l-3.99-4z"/></svg></div></a></div><div class="placeholder xiwykco"><img class="fill-img" src="/assets/img/placeholder-image-69690f.jpg" srcset="/assets/img/placeholder-image-69690f-512w.webp 512w, /assets/img/placeholder-image-69690f-1024w.webp 1024w, /assets/img/placeholder-image-69690f.jpg 1920w" sizes="(min-width: 810px) and (max-width: 1199.98px) 100vw, (max-width: 809.98px) 100vw, 100vw" width="1920" height="1280" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></div></div><div class="x2yd3zd"><div class="placeholder xfj1abc"><img class="fill-img" src="/assets/img/placeholder-image-b57b9e.jpg" srcset="/assets/img/placeholder-image-b57b9e-512w.webp 512w, /assets/img/placeholder-image-b57b9e-1024w.webp 1024w, /assets/img/placeholder-image-b57b9e.jpg 1280w" sizes="(min-width: 810px) and (max-width: 1199.98px) 100vw, (max-width: 809.98px) 100vw, 100vw" width="1280" height="1920" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></div><div class="xokwvh7"><div class="p2 xuszldq"><p class="xspwoe5">Robust Infrastructure</p></div><div class="xkcikp3"><div class="bullet-point x6idugm"><div class="icon xyojafn"><div class="material x8n8qcu"><svg fill="rgb(120, 120, 120)" width="100%" height="100%" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M9 16.17 4.83 12l-1.42 1.41L9 19 21 7l-1.41-1.41z"/></svg></div></div><p class="xv3l5jr">20+ global PoPs and IDCs across Asia-Pacific, EMEA and the Americas</p></div><div class="bullet-point x6idugm"><div class="icon xyojafn"><div class="material x8n8qcu"><svg fill="rgb(120, 120, 120)" width="100%" height="100%" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M9 16.17 4.83 12l-1.42 1.41L9 19 21 7l-1.41-1.41z"/></svg></div></div><p class="xv3l5jr">Owned MPLS/VPLS backbone with direct cloud connectivity</p></div><div class="bullet-point x6idugm"><div class="icon xyojafn"><div class="material x8n8qcu"><svg fill="rgb(120, 120, 120)" width="100%" height="100%" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M9 16.17 4.83 12l-1.42 1.41L9 19 21 7l-1.41-1.41z"/></svg></div></div><p class="xv3l5jr">Carrier-neutral IDC footprint hosting AI-ready compute</p></div></div><a class="link-button xprmn1s" href="/vocom-services"><p class="x9uyvup">Explore Vocom’s Services</p><div class="material x3b1erb"><svg fill="rgb(13, 13, 13)" width="100%" height="100%" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M16.01 11H4v2h12.01v3L20 12l-3.99-4z"/></svg></div></a></div></div></div></div></div><div class="8 xh2uytg" id="ecosystem"><div class="h2 xlsdbpm" id="service"><div class="xrebnwx"><h3 class="h3 x10uerp">Circuits and the Services Around Them</h3><p class="x1shyid">Everything a point-to-point build needs, from one carrier:</p></div></div><div class="xsux5dz"><a class="x8nee5a" href="/vocom-services"><img class="fill-img" src="/assets/img/vocom-international-c6d6eb.jpg" srcset="/assets/img/vocom-international-c6d6eb-512w.webp 512w, /assets/img/vocom-international-c6d6eb-1024w.webp 1024w, /assets/img/vocom-international-c6d6eb.jpg 1282w" sizes="(min-width: 810px) and (max-width: 1199.98px) 100vw, (max-width: 809.98px) 100vw, 100vw" width="1282" height="1920" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><div class="p2 xlxn3qc"><div class="xo4ml8w"><p class="xx7nktr">IEPL</p><p class="x2ad7rc">International Ethernet Private Line: an Ethernet handoff on dedicated transport, scaled in Ethernet increments, often by a configuration change rather than a new circuit.</p></div></div></a><a class="xg6he0s" href="/vocom-services"><img class="fill-img" src="/assets/img/vocom-international-ef085d.jpg" srcset="/assets/img/vocom-international-ef085d-512w.webp 512w, /assets/img/vocom-international-ef085d-1024w.webp 1024w, /assets/img/vocom-international-ef085d.jpg 1920w" sizes="(min-width: 810px) and (max-width: 1199.98px) 100vw, (max-width: 809.98px) 100vw, 100vw" width="1920" height="1280" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><div class="p2 xlxn3qc"><div class="xo4ml8w"><p class="xx7nktr">IPLC</p><p class="x2ad7rc">International Private Leased Circuit on TDM over SDH or SONET, with guaranteed capacity, very low jitter and native E1 or T1 handoff for legacy equipment.</p></div></div></a><div class="x7yt7bq"><a class="xv9tkel" href="/vocom-services"><img class="fill-img" src="/assets/img/vocom-international-15f76d.jpg" srcset="/assets/img/vocom-international-15f76d-512w.webp 512w, /assets/img/vocom-international-15f76d-1024w.webp 1024w, /assets/img/vocom-international-15f76d.jpg 1920w" sizes="(min-width: 810px) and (max-width: 1199.98px) 100vw, (max-width: 809.98px) 100vw, 100vw" width="1920" height="1280" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><div class="p2 xlxn3qc"><div class="xo4ml8w"><p class="xx7nktr">Local Loop</p><p class="x2ad7rc">Local access into Vocom's PoPs for the last mile of a private circuit.</p></div></div></a><a class="xv9tkel" href="/vocom-services"><img class="fill-img" src="/assets/img/vocom-international-dd153d.jpg" srcset="/assets/img/vocom-international-dd153d-512w.webp 512w, /assets/img/vocom-international-dd153d-1024w.webp 1024w, /assets/img/vocom-international-dd153d.jpg 1920w" sizes="(min-width: 810px) and (max-width: 1199.98px) 100vw, (max-width: 809.98px) 100vw, 100vw" width="1920" height="1282" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><div class="p2 xlxn3qc"><div class="xo4ml8w"><p class="xx7nktr">Protected Routes</p><p class="x2ad7rc">Protected paths on major routes, including Hong Kong to Taipei, Singapore, Tokyo and Los Angeles, with estimated round-trip times quoted per route.</p></div></div></a><a class="xv9tkel" href="/vocom-services"><img class="fill-img" src="/assets/img/vocom-international-74f851.jpg" srcset="/assets/img/vocom-international-74f851-512w.webp 512w, /assets/img/vocom-international-74f851-1024w.webp 1024w, /assets/img/vocom-international-74f851.jpg 1080w" sizes="(min-width: 810px) and (max-width: 1199.98px) 100vw, (max-width: 809.98px) 100vw, 100vw" width="1080" height="1080" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><div class="p2 xlxn3qc"><div class="xo4ml8w"><p class="xx7nktr">MPLS-VPN</p><p class="x2ad7rc">An owned MPLS/VPLS backbone with direct cloud connectivity into AWS, Azure and Microsoft.</p></div></div></a><a class="xv9tkel" href="/vocom-services"><img class="fill-img" src="/assets/img/vocom-international-b5a705.jpg" srcset="/assets/img/vocom-international-b5a705-512w.webp 512w, /assets/img/vocom-international-b5a705-1024w.webp 1024w, /assets/img/vocom-international-b5a705.jpg 1920w" sizes="(min-width: 810px) and (max-width: 1199.98px) 100vw, (max-width: 809.98px) 100vw, 100vw" width="1920" height="960" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><div class="p2 xlxn3qc"><div class="xo4ml8w"><p class="xx7nktr">IP Transit and DIA</p><p class="x2ad7rc">Local peering blended with global BGP across 20+ PoPs, including a dedicated China route by carrier.</p></div></div></a></div><a class="xg6he0s" href="/vocom-services"><img class="fill-img" src="/assets/img/vocom-international-cc0050.jpg" srcset="/assets/img/vocom-international-cc0050-512w.webp 512w, /assets/img/vocom-international-cc0050-1024w.webp 1024w, /assets/img/vocom-international-cc0050.jpg 1920w" sizes="(min-width: 810px) and (max-width: 1199.98px) 100vw, (max-width: 809.98px) 100vw, 100vw" width="1920" height="1280" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><div class="p2 xlxn3qc"><div class="xo4ml8w"><p class="xx7nktr">24/7 NOC Monitoring</p><p class="x2ad7rc">The same NOC watches private circuits, IP transit and MPLS around the clock.</p></div></div></a><a class="x8nee5a" href="/vocom-services"><img class="fill-img" src="/assets/img/vocom-international-3ff171.jpg" srcset="/assets/img/vocom-international-3ff171-512w.webp 512w, /assets/img/vocom-international-3ff171-1024w.webp 1024w, /assets/img/vocom-international-3ff171.jpg 1920w" sizes="(min-width: 810px) and (max-width: 1199.98px) 100vw, (max-width: 809.98px) 100vw, 100vw" width="1920" height="1280" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><div class="p2 xlxn3qc"><div class="xo4ml8w"><p class="xx7nktr">Anti-DDoS Protection</p><p class="x2ad7rc">Regional scrubbing centers across Asia and the US/EU keep volumetric and application-layer attacks off the route.</p></div></div></a></div></div><div class="netmap-wrap"><NetworkMap /></div><div class="section-divider xbstc8l"><div class="x2h0iev"></div><div class="xqo6eaw"></div><div class="x2h0iev"></div></div><div class="4 xs4tdkn"><div class="xmrbb9j"><h3 class="h3 x10uerp">Vocom by the Numbers</h3><p class="xq9pbwc">One carrier-grade backbone, three business lines:</p></div><div class="xgbie5l"><div class="xkgm4hh masonry"><div class="xuqg4y9"><h5 class="h5 xxzf2ey">1998</h5><p class="xfxcabm">Founded, FCC 214 Licensed</p></div><div class="xd6smxn"><h5 class="h5 xxzf2ey">20+</h5><p class="xfxcabm">Global PoPs and IDCs</p></div><div class="xd6smxn"><h5 class="h5 xxzf2ey">3</h5><p class="xfxcabm">Core Business Lines</p></div><div class="xd6smxn"><h5 class="h5 xxzf2ey">24/7</h5><p class="xfxcabm">NOC Monitoring</p></div></div></div></div><div class="section-divider xbstc8l"><div class="x2h0iev"></div><div class="xqo6eaw"></div><div class="x2h0iev"></div></div><div class="carousel xctiiw2"><div class="h2 xwpnaea"><div class="xmyyotj"><h3 class="h3 x10uerp">Frequently Asked Questions</h3><p class="xq9pbwc">We are here to clear your doubts:</p></div></div><div class="xgjzcho"><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xzkh4c6"><FaqItem question="What is the difference between IEPL and IPLC?">Both are dedicated point-to-point circuits with the same privacy. IPLC runs on TDM over SDH or SONET, with a native TDM handoff and protection switching in under 50 milliseconds. IEPL presents an Ethernet interface, scales in Ethernet increments and suits traffic that is already IP-native. Our <a href="/blog/plc-vs-iepl" class="text-link">IPLC vs IEPL guide</a> covers the choice in depth.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xzkh4c6"><FaqItem question="What bandwidth options are available?">Circuits are sized to the traffic profile you send us, from sub-1 Gbps access links up to 10 Gbps and above for high-capacity routes such as India to Australia.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xzkh4c6"><FaqItem question="Which routes do you cover?">Cross-Pacific and Asia-Pacific routes, including India to Australia and other APAC point-to-point lanes, from 20+ PoPs and IDCs. Hong Kong to Taipei, Singapore, Tokyo and Los Angeles are among the protected routes.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xzkh4c6"><FaqItem question="Is an Ethernet Private Line the same as an Ethernet Virtual Private Line?">No. An Ethernet Private Line is dedicated and port-based. An Ethernet Virtual Private Line shares a physical port across several logical connections. The names are close and the products are not, so confirm in writing which one a quotation covers.</FaqItem></div><div class="faq-accordian-item-2 xzkh4c6"><FaqItem question="How do I get a quote?">Send the two endpoints, the bandwidth you need and the handoff your equipment expects through the <a href="/contact-vocomai" class="text-link">contact page</a>, and we will return a sized quote.</FaqItem></div></div></div><div class="simple-footer-2 xzxrxrs footer-slot" data-pagefind-ignore><Footer footerTagline="Your partner for telecommunications and fiber optic supply." title="Quick Links" menu1="VOCOM AI" menu2="Services" menu3="RenOS AI Agents" link2="/vocom-services" link3="/vocom-ai-agents" /></div></div>
</Base>
